    "public-key binding rejects missing or substituted keys still accepted by hash and nonce checks",
    "public-key binding requires the actual payer address rather than an independently valid key",
    "public-key binding preserves canonical key syntax empty-signature and exact-field requirements",
    "public-key byte mapping does not establish curve validity key possession or signing authority",
    "key and price binding consumes the same original hash nonce intent and selected Plasma fields",
    "matching public bytes cannot replace the independently selected payment or original allocation",
    "matching public bytes do not bypass nonce validation or original quote price-window guards",
    "public-key APIs reject hostile key address context descriptors proxies and providers without callbacks",
    "public-key APIs enforce exact arity phases and receipt separation without resetting authority",
    "key and price binding retains detached pre-await public bytes without rereading mutated caller input",
    "public-key module remains a fixed-size opt-in hash mapping without key signature or runtime machinery"
